  "conclusions": [
    "Native model performance has not improved in this run; broader fixed controls now expose weaknesses before tuning.",
    "Across the two new Gironde anchors, metric-free candidates cover36.53% disc/29.52% vehicle/36.54% strip pixels with4.99/4.86/5.36 RGB MAE. These are different target masks from earlier reports, not before/after gains.",
    "On accepted textured pixels, above20 RGB-error tails are17.19% disc,9.45% vehicle,17.31% strip despite only2.91%/2.10%/3.82% tails overall. Low-texture asphalt conceals important failures.",
    "Two-view policy reduces coverage to2.57%/3.55%/5.64%, with lower observed tails, but donor agreement still is not independently calibrated geometric reliability.",
    "Same accepted Gironde pixels: source transfer beats Telea on this expanded opaque/strip subset but still worsens blur versus unchanged input,4.99 versus3.76 MAE. Earlier original Gironde strip control favored Telea. Neither can be advertised as universal.",
    "Real Gironde footprint support is58.79% and19.49% projected,75.81% and20.32% angular; two-view support25.16% and0%. This measures availability only, with no clean under-car truth.",
    "Nantes and Bourges still produce zero controlled and natural coverage at all four new anchors. Their four windows admit only2 of220 unique masked pair proposals, so another unchanged geometry-only fit is not justified.",
    "All nine anchors are reused development/train. No held-out route image was read or scored. Controlled patches cover substantially smaller angular cones than the real ego masks."
